{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "21", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "24", "S": "18"}}, "news": [{"title": "Odisha housing department speeds up hearings on building plan appeals", "para": "The housing department of Odisha is making strides in addressing building plan violations and disputes by conducting intensified hearings. A significant number of appeals have been pending since 2002, yet the department is focusing on both older and recent issues pertaining to planning regulations. This initiative is essential for boosting transparency while tackling the considerable backlog of cases, crucial for adhering to urban planning standards and discouraging future violations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/odisha-housing-department-speeds-up-hearings-on-building-plan-appeals/133393368?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-204202/133393368.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Developers employing 50 or more workers at Noida construction sites get 15 days to set up cr\u00e8ches", "para": "The Noida administration has mandated that construction sites establish cr\u00e8ches within a strict timeline of fifteen days. This initiative comes in response to growing concerns for children's well-being amidst construction activities. Facilities must maintain cleanliness and hygiene, distance from potential hazards, and ensure staff are police-verified.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/developers-employing-50-or-more-workers-at-noida-construction-sites-get-15-days-to-set-up-crches/133392094?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-292878/133392094.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}, {"title": "Regularise minor building violations: Plea seeks one-time relief policy for Sushant Lok 1, 2 and 3", "para": "Residents of Sushant Lok are advocating for a dedicated policy addressing minor building deviations. This initiative seeks to formalize technical irregularities while safeguarding genuine buyers. Advocates argue that it's unjust to classify unsuspecting purchasers as intentional lawbreakers. A proposed composition system could not only generate funds but also offer legal clarity, potentially resolving a significant administrative challenge for many families.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/regularise-minor-building-violations-plea-seeks-one-time-relief-policy-for-sushant-lok-1-2-and-3/133392025?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-143334/133392025.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}